        "Content": "The Property Shop are delighted to present this truly impressive home to the Dublin 7 Market. Number 19 St David`s Terrace is a spacious 3 bedroom family home situated at the junction of Blackhorse Avenue and the NCR, just on the edge of the ever  popular village of Stoneybatter. Homes of this size and quality are a real find in this location, and will appeal to those currently living in the area and looking to trade up to a more sizeable home. Number 19 offers generous and light filled accommodation. The accommodation on the ground floor comprises of; entrance hall, open plan large living/dining rooms, connecting to the dine in extended kitchen to the side, a utility and shower room to the rear. On the first floor there are two spacious double bedrooms, one single bedroom and a large family bathroom, the attic has been converted, currently used as a home office. There is a Northwest facing patio garden to the rear with pedestrian access from a gated lane way.The property is well positioned within a short stroll of Stoneybatter village, with an abundance of independent shops, cafes, bars and restaurants, a real food lovers destination. The village has a real sense of community with residents enjoying a very relaxed atmosphere and a village to be proud of. Smithfield Village, The Phoenix Park, TU Dublin Grangegorman and the City Centre are also all within easy walking distance. There is also a number of National & Secondary schools in the area including the D7 Educate Together at Grangegorman. The area is well serviced by Dublin Bus and the Luas. Viewing is highly recommended and by appointment only through our Manor Street office.\r\n\r\nHallway 8m (26'3\") x 1.5m (4'11\")\r\nLong welcoming hallway with pattern quarry tile floor, high ceilings with coving and ceiling rose, cast iron radiator, under stair storage.\r\n\r\nLiving/Dining 8m (26'3\") x 3.4m (11'2\")\r\nBright and spacious interconnecting rooms with matching feature fire places, high ceilings with coving & ceiling roses, dual aspect, walnut wood floors, built in shelving.  A fantastic place to relax, dine & entertain.\r\n\r\nKitchen 4.5m (14'9\") x 3.1m (10'2\")\r\nOff the main living room a fully fitted kitchen with room to dine, ample floor & wall units, integrated dishwasher, 5 ring gas range/oven, vaulted ceilings with beams, Velux windows, continuation of the walnut floor combined with tiles, tiled surround.\r\n\r\nUtility 2.3m (7'7\") x 1.9m (6'3\")\r\nLarge utility area, plumbed for laundry, plenty of storage, tiled floor, access to the rear yard.\r\n\r\nShower Room 2m (6'7\") x 1.04m (3'5\")\r\nOff the utility a recently refurbished shower room with tiled floor & surround, corner shower unit, WC & WHB.\r\n\r\nBathroom 2.3m (7'7\") x 3.5m (11'6\")\r\nLocated on the upstairs return, a full family bathroom with tiled floor & surround, corner shower unit, free standing roll top bath , extractor fan, WHB with vanity, WC.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 4.1m (13'5\") x 3.7m (12'2\")\r\nLocated to the rear of the property, a spacious double bedroom with original wood flooring, built in wardrobes and high ceilings.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 3.9m (12'10\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nA light filled double bedroom to the front of the property, with original painted wood flooring, built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 3.2m (10'6\") x 1.9m (6'3\")\r\nA large single bedroom located to the front of the property.\r\n\r\nAttic Room 3.7m (12'2\") x 2.9m (9'6\")\r\nA great addition to the home, currently set up as a home office, could have many different uses, accessed by a wooden staircase, Velux windows and under eave storage.\r\n\r\nExterior 5m (16'5\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\r\nLarge NW facing patio garden with plenty of room to relax, rear access to a gated lane way.\r\nOn street resident`s disc parking available.\r\n\r\nArea \r\nApprox 114 Sq M (125 Sq M to include Attic)"
      },
